Build **Wireworm**, a fixed-shooter arcade game with a charged-terrain discharge
system that runs entirely in the browser.

Your project root is `{{workspace}}`. Create the game there.

## Your starting point

A starter project is already in place at `{{workspace}}`: a `package.json` that
pins **Playwright** as a dev dependency, and an `assets/` folder of the game's
sprite art. Its dependencies have already been installed for you —
`node_modules/` is populated and Playwright's headless **Chromium** is downloaded
— so you can build and verify right away. Build on this project rather than
replacing it: keep the `package.json`, add your framework, bundler, and a `build`
script on top of it, and keep the lockfile in sync (see below).

## What to read first

The full specification is split across the files below, all already present in
your project. Read every one of them before you start, then implement the game
they describe as a single, cohesive build:

{{#each specs}}
- `{{this.path}}`
